                    insight_closed:         `Mandate closed coherently: ROIC reached ≥16% and growth ≥8% on the back of a committed direction whose control system and capital pattern all reinforce each other. The strategy became behaviour, not a slide.`,
                    insight_incoherent:     `The numbers landed but the plan is incoherent: you hedged somewhere — direction, incentives or capital — so the result is fragile and the board will distrust it. A strategy the organisation isn't aligned behind rarely holds.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You met the mandate but strategic fit is thin. Without a control system and capital pattern that genuinely reinforce the direction, the gains are unlikely to compound into Year 2 and 3.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the 8%/16% mandate. In group language that triggers a strategic review — a divestment candidate. Re-examine where the strategy failed to become a measured, funded, rewarded job.`,
                    insight_hedged:         `You hedged rather than committed — funding or rewarding a bit of everything. With €48M against €78M of demand, straddling under-resources the real bet and wins at none.`,
                    insight_overspent:      `Your plan committed more than the €48M envelope. Group will not reverse the cut, so the over-spend is a wish-list, not an allocation — the first thing the board strips out.`,
                    insight_lowfit:         `Strategic fit stayed low: strategy, control system and capital did not line up. This is Gibbons' core warning — a direction not embedded in the planning and control system never becomes real behaviour.`,
                    insight_embedded:       `This strategy is embedded, not announced: a single committed direction, incentives realigned across the three functions, a focused scorecard the parent will use, and capital concentrated behind the bet. It survives the handover to next year's plan.`,

                    hint_hedged:            `You're hedging — funding or rewarding a bit of all three archetypes. Commit the division to one direction and concentrate incentives and capital behind it.`,
